  "title": { "en": "Arriving at Barajas", "es": "Llegar a Barajas" },
  "objectives": [
    "Get through passport control: the reason for your trip",
    "Find your bags and your terminal",
    "Ask how to get to the centre, and choose metro, bus or taxi"
  ],
  "teach": [
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "¿Motivo del viaje? — Turismo. Cuatro días.", "en": "Reason for your trip? — Tourism. Four days.", "note": "At el control de pasaportes, arriving from outside the Schengen area. Short answers are perfect. Officers often switch to English." },
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "¿Dónde está la recogida de equipajes?", "en": "Where's baggage claim?", "note": "el equipaje = luggage. Screens show your flight and a belt number." },
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "Llego a la terminal cuatro.", "en": "I arrive at terminal 4.", "note": "la terminal is feminine. Barajas has T1, T2, T3 and the separate T4. Which one depends on your airline." },
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "Perdone, ¿cómo voy al centro?", "en": "Excuse me, how do I get to the centre?", "note": "voy = I go (ir). The information desk will give you the options below." },
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "md": "**Barajas to the centre:**\n\n- **Metro, line 8** (pink) to Nuevos Ministerios, then change. Airport stations charge **el suplemento del aeropuerto**, an extra €3 on top of the ticket.\n- **Exprés Aeropuerto** bus: €5, runs 24 hours, to Atocha (to Cibeles at night).\n- **Cercanías** train from T4 to Atocha and Chamartín.\n- **Taxi**: the fixed €33 to anywhere inside the M-30 (day 50)."
    }
  ],
